    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2W7uYsAaeDDpMeMr9D7jFJS)_\n\n## Merge order\n- Independent: touches only `sp-litnotes-meta` (doc, `.el`, tests); no stacked PRs.\n- Branch name has no PR number yet (rename to `<PR>-litnote-create-template` before review if wanted).\n\n## Cause\n- `sp-litnotes-meta--around-create` makes the note itself only when `sp-litnotes-meta--entry` finds the key.\n- `--entry` parsed the .bib with `bibtex-parse-entry`, which returns nil for an entry type the buffer's dialect lacks (`@online`, `@thesis`, `@video`, `@news`...). Reproduced in batch.\n- Such an entry looked missing, so the advice silently fell back to citar's own template: `#+title: Notes on ...` and `#+print_bibliography:`, no ID/tags/CREATED, no title per `sp-litnotes-titles`.\n- Explains why only some articles are affected. It got visible after the BibLaTeX/new-type entries (#sp-bibtex-biblatex, 2026-11-15). The history of the advice is squashed in merge commits, so I could not bisect to one commit.\n- Not the cause: #534, #542, sp-see-also, sp-note-kinds.\n\n## Changes\n- Every entry type is read (`sp-litnotes-meta--bibtex-mode`, dialect extended by the buffer's types).\n- Citar's template is never used for a new note (your \"always prefer my personal template\"): missing entry or failing create = visible error; existing note for the key is visited.\n- New title: editors when no authors (`(ed.)` suffix per `sp-litnotes-titles`), organisations kept whole, `sp-litnotes-titles-format-function`.\n- `#+print_bibliography:` is not written (decision of #338). You wrote \"keeps the print_bibliography\", read as \"it keeps adding it\"; tell me if you want it written instead.\n- Doc: `docs/tangles/academic/sp-litnotes-meta.org` (bullets). Tests: 5 new ERT tests. 5 other tests in that file already fail in the cloud container (report buffers), unchanged.\n\n## Manual testing\n- [ ] `C-; B c` on a key whose entry is `@online`/`@thesis`: note has ID, CREATED, ROAM_REFS, tags, title `Last (Year) Title`, filled meta with links, no `print_bibliography`\n- [ ] Same for an article-type key (still fine)\n- [ ] Editor-only book: title `Lee (ed.) (2001) Title`\n- [ ] Organisation author: title not cut to `Bank (2020)`\n- [ ] Key that already has a note: it is opened, no second file\n- [ ] Key not in the registered .bib files: error message, no file\n- [ ] `M-x sp-check-tangle` clean\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBzRgz7HiCb4sPpKbk)_",
